turning back to the u.s we have some  good news out of texas where a  three-year-old boy who was lost in the  woods for three days was found alive and  safe christopher ramirez returned to his  mother on saturday following an intense  search near his home outside of houston  he was found by a neighbor who heard  about the search and decided to help  omar villafranca has more  this is the moment christopher ramirez  and his mother reunited after he had  been missing for three days great news  he is alive and well the three-year-old  was last seen wednesday in grimes county  texas when his mother says he chased the  family's dog into the woods  his mother desperately pleaded with the  public to help find her son saying that  she had only taken her eyes off him for  two minutes before he vanished  members of the community along with more  than 200 law enforcement officials the  fbi and search crews scoured the area  for days and nights with no luck there's  not normally a situation where you have  a three-year-old child who has gone  almost 72 hours with no food no water no  shelter but then after three days of  searching around the clock an  unbelievable discovery the child was  found alive he is alive he's thirsty  he's with his mother and he's going to  the hospital  praise the lord  yes sir again police got a call from a  nearby landowner who went looking for  the boy the man found christopher in the  woods about five miles from where he  disappeared and said the toddler was  naked but appeared calm and unhurt we  never lost faith and we never lost hope  in the fact that christopher would be  found  i'm proud to say we accomplished that  for cbs mornings i'm omar villafranca in  fort worth texas
 

